      "lineNbr": 136,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-22T12:29:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is UB as you re-interpret the bytes with varying signedness and widths.\n\nInstead, I\u0027d recommend using safe conversions and operations e.g.\n```\nfn from_signed_offset(offset: isize, max_offset: usize) -\u003e Option\u003cusize\u003e {\n    offset.try_into().ok().or(max_offset.checked_add_signed(offset))\n}\n```\nthen\n```\nlet offset \u003d if Some(offset) \u003d from_signed_offset(offset, kernel.len()) {\n    offset\n} else {\n    return // ...\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 136,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "a96dbe66522cdd0a34931a8752622d9162d370a1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d59e654_dec1b410",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-22T12:29:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could let the slice handle bounds checking using `.get()` and should validate that the range doesn\u0027t wrap with `offset.checked_add(num_bytes)`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 137,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "a96dbe66522cdd0a34931a8752622d9162d370a1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3246834d_e6c0d0d3",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
